The cell 'span verbatim in the document / value a substring of the span' specifies that the span is exactly present in the document and the value is a substring of that span. For the kernel `conformance.kernel.grounding`, the rule states it provides the grounding verdict with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" [6ab8417a77f3b613]. In the input, the span "The red fox" is verbatim in the document and the value "red fox" is a substring of that span; the rule implies a verdict of GROUNDED. In the rewritten text, I change the value to "blue fox", which is no longer a substring of the span. The rule then implies a verdict of VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN. Thus, the verdict moves.